# Enterprise Campus Network

A Cisco Packet Tracer enterprise campus network designed to demonstrate
VLAN segmentation, Layer 2 redundancy, Layer 3 routing, and network
availability.

## Technologies

- VLANs
- Inter-VLAN Routing
- STP / Rapid PVST+
- PortFast
- BPDU Guard
- EtherChannel
- OSPF
- DHCP
- Multilayer Switching
- Layer 2 / Layer 3 Design

## VLANs

| VLAN | Network |
|------|---------|
| 10 | 192.168.10.0/24 |
| 20 | 192.168.20.0/24 |
| 30 | 192.168.30.0/24 |
| 40 | 192.168.40.0/24 |

## STP Design

The network uses Rapid PVST+ for Layer 2 redundancy.

- Multilayer Switch 0: Root Bridge for VLANs 10 and 30
- Multilayer Switch 1: Root Bridge for VLAN 20
- Access switches use PortFast and BPDU Guard on end-device ports.

## Routing

OSPF is configured as the dynamic routing protocol between the
Layer 3 devices.

The routed links use point-to-point addressing.

## DHCP

A dedicated DHCP server provides IP addressing for the VLANs.

## EtherChannel

EtherChannel is configured between the multilayer switches to provide
link redundancy and increased bandwidth.

